{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115870",
      "title": "Analyzing a Built-in Structural Directive: ngIf",
      "lectureOrder": 154,
      "videoOrder": 146,
      "sourceHash": "dc29cda0c103bac9b6a19df3e512ca21356116b7ec21c65c21b587d1a17bde84",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "So, how do structural directives look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "Well, in this application, we have this auth service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "where I manage some dummy auth state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 13.35,
          "en": "So where I, in the end, check the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.35,
          "end": 15.03,
          "en": "for some hardcoded values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.03,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "And depending on which credentials were entered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 20.67,
          "en": "I set the active permission of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.67,
          "end": 23.91,
          "en": "to either admin, user, or guest.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.91,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "And therefore, we could use these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "values here to dynamically show some content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 35.15,
          "en": "so that admins see different content than users and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 38.37,
          "en": "So for example, here in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.37,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "below the auth component, we could add a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 47.073,
          "en": "which only admins should see, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.94,
          "end": 52.11,
          "en": "To make this work, we need to go to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 55.98,
          "en": "TypeScript file and make that service available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.98,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "For that we can inject it, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 62.52,
          "en": "by adding a private property called auth service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.52,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "And by then using the inject function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 67.92,
          "en": "and injecting the auth service like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 69.543,
          "en": "into this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 74.49,
          "en": "And then with that injected, since in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.49,
          "end": 79.49,
          "en": "I managed the active permission in auth service as a signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.65,
          "end": 82.53,
          "en": "we can go back to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.53,
          "end": 85.863,
          "en": "and add a property called isAdmin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.85,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "which could be a computed property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "with help of the computed function provided by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "which can be used on signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "to get this auth service active permission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 100.293,
          "en": "And check if it's equal to admin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.42,
          "end": 105.47999999999999,
          "en": "So that would give us an isAdmin property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 108.75,
          "en": "which we can use in the template of this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.75,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "which is true if the active permission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 114.12299999999999,
          "en": "has a value of admin, and false otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.74000000000001,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "And now in the app component HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "we could use that with @if, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 125.76,
          "en": "to conditionally render this paragraph like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.76,
          "end": 129.48,
          "en": "Though since isAdmin is a signal, we need to execute this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.48,
          "end": 132.213,
          "en": "to read the value and set up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "With that, back in the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 140.82,
          "en": "if we log in with an email of admin@example.com",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.82,
          "end": 143.79,
          "en": "and a password of admin and we click log in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.79,
          "end": 146.883,
          "en": "we should see this conditionally rendered content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.05,
          "end": 151.11,
          "en": "But here, we're not using any directives at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 154.26,
          "en": "Instead we're using this conditional rendering syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.26,
          "end": 156.423,
          "en": "you learned about earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 159.36,
          "en": "Well, but back then I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.36,
          "end": 162.18,
          "en": "that this is a relatively new feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.18,
          "end": 165.39,
          "en": "You can only use this @if syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.39,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "if you are working with Angular 17 or newer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "Prior to that, you had to use a structural directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 176.403,
          "en": "to conditionally render content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.48,
          "end": 181.35,
          "en": "So in older Angular versions, if you wanted to render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.35,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "this paragraph here conditionally, you would've done that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 188.523,
          "en": "by adding the ngIf directive on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 192.09,
          "en": "So another directive coming from Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.09,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "as you can tell by the name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "but now this is a structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "Now, what makes it a structural directive though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 202.44,
          "en": "Well, for one, that you add an asterisk",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.44,
          "end": 204.78,
          "en": "in front of this directive name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.78,
          "end": 208.8,
          "en": "You need to add this when using structural directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.8,
          "end": 211.29,
          "en": "because this will tell Angular that under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 211.29,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "it needs to change that code a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "And you'll see how it would be changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 218.61,
          "en": "a little bit later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.61,
          "end": 221.07,
          "en": "But it's also a structural directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.07,
          "end": 225,
          "en": "because whilst you still do add it like an attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225,
          "end": 228.3,
          "en": "onto this paragraph, if you ignore this asterisk,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.3,
          "end": 232.5,
          "en": "this directive will actually change the structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 232.5,
          "end": 236.04,
          "en": "of the DOM, which the attribute directive did not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.04,
          "end": 240.15,
          "en": "The attribute directive really only changed the behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 240.15,
          "end": 242.04,
          "en": "of this input element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.04,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "This structural directive here, on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.04,
          "end": 247.35,
          "en": "will change the structure of the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.35,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "because it will either render this paragraph or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 252.84,
          "en": "which has an impact on the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.84,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "If an element is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 256.86,
          "en": "that changes the structure of the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.86,
          "end": 259.533,
          "en": "That's why this is called a structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 264,
          "en": "Now, you would then use ngIf by putting your condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264,
          "end": 268.02,
          "en": "between those quotes here, after the equal sign like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 268.02,
          "end": 272.04,
          "en": "And since this is a directive, and not a template feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.04,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "built into Angular, you need to make it available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "in the component you're using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.8,
          "end": 280.35,
          "en": "at least if you're using standalone components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.35,
          "end": 284.34000000000003,
          "en": "And therefore, you would have to import ngIf",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.34000000000003,
          "end": 289.05,
          "en": "from @angular/common, and add it to this imports array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.05,
          "end": 291.753,
          "en": "to unlock it in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 293.43,
          "end": 297.21,
          "en": "But with that, if you reload this and you log in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.21,
          "end": 302.19,
          "en": "as an admin, you would still see this conditional content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 302.19,
          "end": 304.923,
          "en": "but now with help of the structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.18,
          "end": 309.36,
          "en": "Now, again, in modern Angular applications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.36,
          "end": 311.46,
          "en": "you typically wouldn't use that anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.46,
          "end": 314.01,
          "en": "you would instead use this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.01,
          "end": 317.19,
          "en": "But since this module here is about directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 317.19,
          "end": 318.93,
          "en": "I wanted to show you an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 318.93,
          "end": 321.69,
          "en": "for such a structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 321.69,
          "end": 324.39,
          "en": "And it was a super important Angular feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 327.87,
          "en": "in the past of Angular, and still is in projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 327.87,
          "end": 330.633,
          "en": "that are using older Angular versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.47,
          "end": 333.9,
          "en": "Now, why did I pick this example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 333.9,
          "end": 337.08,
          "en": "and not some built-in structural directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 337.08,
          "end": 340.98,
          "en": "which still does matter in modern Angular?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 340.98,
          "end": 344.04,
          "en": "Well, simply because in modern Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 344.04,
          "end": 345.42,
          "en": "there are no built-in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.42,
          "end": 348.45,
          "en": "structural directives left that would matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.45,
          "end": 352.2,
          "en": "We only had ngIf for conditional content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.2,
          "end": 355.62,
          "en": "and ngFor for content that should be output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 355.62,
          "end": 357.51,
          "en": "with help of a loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.51,
          "end": 360.15,
          "en": "But for that, we now have @for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 360.15,
          "end": 362.76,
          "en": "So in modern Angular, there are no built-in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.76,
          "end": 365.55,
          "en": "structural directives left that you would need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.55,
          "end": 368.46,
          "en": "Nonetheless, this feature exists and nonetheless,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.46,
          "end": 370.68,
          "en": "I'll soon show you how you can build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.68,
          "end": 372.84,
          "en": "your own structural directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.84,
          "end": 375.66,
          "en": "For now, it's just important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 375.66,
          "end": 377.43,
          "en": "that the feature exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.43,
          "end": 381.15,
          "en": "And that the difference compared to attribute directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.15,
          "end": 385.11,
          "en": "is that structural directives do change the structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.11,
          "end": 387.483,
          "en": "of the DOM, hence their name.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
